1
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:09,250
If your fist fits under the leg strap, it's too loose.

2
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:11,310
In a fall, you could slip out.

3
00:00:13,210 --> 00:00:16,960
I'm Alpay Oktay, a Class A Occupational Safety Specialist.

4
00:00:17,270 --> 00:00:19,380
Let's fit a full-body harness correctly.

5
00:00:21,120 --> 00:00:24,230
Remember: guardrails and safety nets come first.

6
00:00:24,360 --> 00:00:26,230
The harness is your last resort.

7
00:00:26,410 --> 00:00:27,920
Inspect it before use.

8
00:00:28,070 --> 00:00:29,200
Is the label readable?

9
00:00:29,410 --> 00:00:30,620
Any cuts or burns?

10
00:00:30,810 --> 00:00:32,100
Are the buckles intact?

11
00:00:32,330 --> 00:00:34,420
If in doubt, don't use it.

12
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:37,090
Hold it by the back D-ring.

13
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:38,290
Shake out the straps.

14
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:41,990
Slip it on like a jacket.

15
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:45,410
Fasten the chest strap at mid-chest.

16
00:00:45,700 --> 00:00:48,910
If there are two front fall-arrest loops, clip through both.

17
00:00:50,870 --> 00:00:52,220
Tighten the leg straps.

18
00:00:52,410 --> 00:00:55,270
A flat hand fits, a fist doesn't.

19
00:00:55,290 --> 00:00:57,280
Tuck loose ends into the keepers.

20
00:00:58,780 --> 00:01:02,450
The back D-ring sits between your shoulder blades, not at your waist.

21
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:04,130
Have a coworker check it.

22
00:01:06,170 --> 00:01:12,660
Connect the energy-absorbing lanyard to the back D-ring, and the hook to an approved anchor, above shoulder height if possible.

23
00:01:12,870 --> 00:01:14,300
Check the lock by hand.

24
00:01:16,150 --> 00:01:19,040
Never anchor at foot level, or to pipes.

25
00:01:20,360 --> 00:01:24,290
The energy absorber extends during a fall, so you need enough clearance below.

26
00:01:24,560 --> 00:01:26,470
Check the manufacturer's instructions.

27
00:01:27,770 --> 00:01:30,500
After a fall, take the harness out of service.

28
00:01:30,730 --> 00:01:32,820
Have a rescue plan ready before work.

29
00:01:34,690 --> 00:01:36,440
Who checks the harnesses on your site?

30
00:01:36,550 --> 00:01:37,740
Tell us in the comments.

31
00:01:37,970 --> 00:01:40,300
Reliable information, safer lives.

